complex-numbers needs real-numbers: complex numbers a+ib are built from pairs of reals
complex-numbers relates q-why-nature-uses-complex-numbers: raises: an invented number i ends up governing quantum physics
fundamental-theorem-of-algebra needs complex-numbers: only in complex numbers does every polynomial have a root
cubic-formula needs complex-numbers: with three real roots, Cardano's formula passes through complex intermediate values
power-series needs limits: a power series' value is the limit of its partial sums
divergent-series needs power-series: evaluating a power series beyond convergence gives Euler's 1+4+16+… = −1/3
complex-plane needs complex-numbers: plots z = x+iy as the point (x, y)
poles needs complex-plane: the poles of 1/(1+z²) at ±i lie off the real line
circle-of-convergence needs power-series: a power series converges inside a circle about the origin, diverges outside
circle-of-convergence needs complex-plane: the convergence region is a disc in the complex plane
circle-of-convergence needs poles: the circle's radius reaches out to the nearest singularity
circle-of-convergence relates q-hidden-divergence: addresses: poles at ±i set the convergence radius to 1
mandelbrot-set needs complex-plane: iterates z ↦ z²+c for points c in the complex plane
mandelbrot-set relates q-platonic-world-real: illustrates: its endless intricacy was discovered, not invented by Mandelbrot
q-why-nature-uses-complex-numbers relates complex-numbers: is about: why numbers with i² = −1 underlie physics
q-why-nature-uses-complex-numbers relates q-why-math-describes-physics: is a case of: an invented abstraction matching nature with precision
q-hidden-divergence relates power-series: is about: why the series for 1/(1+x²) fails beyond |x| = 1
poles relates q-hidden-divergence: explains: hidden poles at ±i limit convergence to |x| < 1
