constraint-equations needs canonical-quantum-gravity: constraints on initial 3-surface data become operator conditions on states
constraint-equations needs hamiltonian-formalism: constraints arise because GR's Hamiltonian form has gauge freedom
graviton-helicity needs helicity: graviton helicity is spin about the direction of motion, plus or minus 2
graviton-helicity needs gravitational-waves: gravitons are the quanta of gravitational waves
graviton-helicity needs weyl-tensor: the free Weyl curvature carries the graviton's degrees of freedom
