self-dual-weyl-curvature needs self-dual-field: same F +/- i*F split as Maxwell, now for gravitons' handedness
self-dual-weyl-curvature needs volume-element: the dual is formed by contracting with the volume element epsilon
ashtekar-variables needs canonical-quantum-gravity: new canonical variables that make the gravity constraints polynomial
ashtekar-variables needs two-spinors: uses only the unprimed (one-handed) spin connection
ashtekar-variables needs gauge-connection: the basic variable is a connection, making gravity resemble gauge theory
barbero-immirzi-parameter needs ashtekar-variables: replaces the i in Ashtekar's connection by a real parameter eta
barbero-immirzi-parameter needs two-spinors: the spin group becomes compact while losing the self-dual chirality
barbero-immirzi-parameter needs unitary-group: turns the noncompact SL(2,C) into the compact SU(2)
wilson-loops needs parallel-transport: parallel transport of spinors around a closed loop
wilson-loops needs gauge-connection: the holonomy of the connection around a loop
wilson-loops needs trace: taking the trace makes the holonomy basis-independent
loop-variables needs wilson-loops: Wilson loops are the basic variables, giving states on loops
loop-variables needs ashtekar-variables: Wilson loops of Ashtekar's connection make the loop representation
loop-variables needs dirac-delta-function: loop states have delta-function support concentrated on the loops
area-quantization needs loop-variables: area counts the loop crossings of the probe surface
area-quantization needs barbero-immirzi-parameter: eta enters the area formula 8 pi G eta hbar sqrt(j(j+1))
jones-polynomial needs knots-and-links: the polynomials are invariants distinguishing knots and links
jones-polynomial needs abstract-index-notation: Kauffman's diagrammatic algebra extends the binor diagram notation
q-deformation needs jones-polynomial: deforms the binor calculus by q = A^2 from the Kauffman bracket
q-deformation needs lie-algebra: so-called quantum groups are deformations of Lie group structure
topological-quantum-field-theory needs quantum-field-theory: QFT with no local degrees of freedom, only global topological data
topological-quantum-field-theory needs knots-and-links: Witten's TQFT yields knot invariants such as the Jones polynomial
spin-networks needs spin: each line is a total-spin unit, combined by angular-momentum rules
spin-networks needs loop-variables: loop-variable states with intersections organize into spin networks
spin-networks needs epr-bohm: illustrated by combining two EPR-Bohm spin-0 pairs, giving rational probabilities
black-hole-entropy-loop needs spin-networks: counts spin-network edges piercing the horizon
black-hole-entropy-loop needs bekenstein-hawking-entropy: the count must reproduce S = A/4
