noncommutative-geometry needs canonical-commutation-relations: noncommuting algebras like [p, x] = i hbar define quantum 'spaces'
twistor-correspondence needs light-cones: an event corresponds to the set of light rays on its light cone
twistor-correspondence needs celestial-sphere: an event's celestial sphere of rays becomes a Riemann sphere in PN
twistor-correspondence needs riemann-sphere: each spacetime event is represented by a Riemann sphere
