robinson-congruence needs projective-twistor-space: a point of PT+ or PT- gives a twisting light-ray family
robinson-congruence needs clifford-parallels: at fixed time its rays project to the Clifford-parallel Hopf circles
alpha-planes needs twistors: each twistor corresponds to an alpha-plane via the incidence relation
alpha-planes needs complexified-minkowski-space: alpha-planes are complex null 2-planes in complexified Minkowski space
alpha-planes needs self-dual-field: their tangent bivectors are self-dual, beta-planes anti-self-dual
twistor-quantization needs twistors: twistor Z and conjugate Z-bar become non-commuting operators
twistor-quantization needs canonical-quantization: Z-bar acts as -d/dZ, like momentum as a derivative
twistor-quantization needs holomorphic-functions: twistor wavefunctions depend on Z alone, hence holomorphic
